# Built-in logical init unit anchor (plan §1.3(9)).
#
# In M0 this was a no-op placeholder: the first-wave mounts are hardcoded in
# the binary. From M1 the unit directory is parsed, so this is the first node
# of the dependency graph.
#
# `Type=target` in `[Unit]` marks a process-less aggregation point (plan §7.2).
# It is a *different* key from `[Service] Type=` (simple|oneshot|notify): the
# parser locates keys by "section + key", so the two never collide. Both this
# `Type=target` and the `.target` suffix identify this as a target; a file
# whose suffix and `Type=` disagree is rejected fail-closed rather than
# silently overridden (plan §1.1).
[Unit]
Description=rinit system initialization
Type=target
